Python File Handling – Advance Practice Questions

These exercises are designed to help to practice Python file handling concepts including
reading files, writing files, append mode.
---

Write a program to read a file and print only those lines which contain the word 'Python'.

---

Write a program to count the total number of characters present in a file.

---

Write a program that reads a file and prints each line with its line number.

---

Write a program that writes numbers from 1 to 20 into a file and then reads the file to print only even numbers.

---

Write a program that stores student marks in a file and then reads the file to find the student with the highest marks.

---

Write a program that copies the contents of one file into another file.

---

Write a program that reads a file and counts how many times a specific word appears.

---

Write a program that removes blank lines from a file and writes the cleaned content into a new file.
---